# ACTUAL OWNERSHIP MODEL (2026-09): SOLE OWNER + one independent four-eyes
# reviewer. The former multi-team owners (architects, compliance, dpo, legal,
# platform, security, web-team) never existed and have been REMOVED: GitHub marks
# unknown teams as invalid owners and, with "require review from Code Owners"
# enabled, that would permanently block every pull request.
#
# FOUR-EYES (two-person integrity):
#   * The owner authors PRs. @IterVitae (the owner's son — an independent GitHub
#     account) is the required reviewer. GitHub forbids self-approval, so
#     @IterVitae's approval IS the four-eyes gate on every change.
#   * @IterVitae MUST be added as a repo collaborator (or Via-Vitae org member)
#     or GitHub shows "unknown owner" and the rule does not resolve.
#   * @IterVitae must use HIS OWN credentials. If the owner also holds that
#     login, the four-eyes control is void (self-approval) and breaches GitHub
#     account-sharing terms.
#   * OWNER: add your own handle to the default rule when convenient, e.g.
#         *   @JourneyOfLife   @IterVitae
#     (guidance in a comment, not a placeholder rule, so CI never sees a fake owner).
#
# LIMITS OF THIS CONTROL (recorded honestly — see README launch gates):
#   * GitHub enforces code review only. For GDPR Article-9 / DPIA / legal /
#     payment / auth changes a family reviewer is NOT independent or necessarily
#     competent assurance; those paths ALSO require off-platform DPO /
#     external-expert sign-off before merge or go-live.
#   * Branch protection = required status checks + required Code Owner review,
#     with admin bypass ON so the sole owner is never locked out when the
#     reviewer is unavailable (every bypass is logged and visible).
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins; guarded paths are declared after broad ones.

